 "text": "9/29/26, 9:39 AM\nWhen you display the move-in documents for a business partner or a premise, the documents from the last three months appear.\nIf no documents exist for this period then the system displays the documents from the last six months.\n\nOnce you have entered the move-in, move-out, or move-in/out, you can use the SAP Business Workflows to trigger and monitor\nadditional business processes.\n\nYou can re-process incomplete move-ins and monitor the status of processing. This may be necessary if, for example:\ne The meter readings are unavailable\ne The budget billing plan cannot be created, or\ne The data required to print the welcome letter is incomplete\n\nMove-In Charges\n\nWhen you save the move-in document, the system posts the move-in charges automatically, provided you have configured the\nsystem accordingly in Customizing under |)*Move-In/Out \u00bb Define System Parameters for Move-In and Move-Out.\n\nYou can configure the system to post the charges to a contract or contract account. You configure how the system calculates the\ncharges using the parameters Charge category and Charge schema. In this way, you can, for example, levy a move-in charge\n\nstaggered to correspond with the number of contracts.\nReduced Layouts\n\nIn Customizing, you can define reduced layouts for the configurable tab on page on the move-in screen to hide some of the data on\nthe individual tab pages. The layouts can now be stored in the special processing variants for the move-in/out. This enables agents\nto process move-ins and move-in/outs more quickly.\n\nBudget Billing\n\nA budget billing amount agreed with the customer is also taken in account if the move-in is entered by the master data generator.\nIf a budget billing plan cannot be created for a contact in move-in processing then the BudgetBillingPlansFailed event of the\nMOVEINDOC BOR object type is triggered.\n\nActivity Log\n\nIn Customizing you can configure the system to save the activity log for the move-in. You can then display it on the move-in screen.\nTo do this choose |}*Extras \u00bb Display Activity Log.\n\nActivities\nInitial Screen\n\nBased on the data you specified on the initial screen, the system automatically determines which of the following cases applies:\n\nExists before move-in                                      Is created during move-in\nBusiness partner, contract account, installation | Contract\n\nBusiness partner, installation                           Contract account, contract\n",
